      "text": "The given sequence is an arithmetic series with a common difference of $6$. The first term is $1$, and the last term is $259$. To find the number of terms in the series, we use the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic series, which is $a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d$, where $a_n$ is the last term, $a_1$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $n$ is the number of terms. So we have:\n\n\\[\n259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6\n\\]\n\nSolving for $n$:\n\n\\[\n259 = 1 + 6n - 6 \\implies 259 = 6n - 5 \\implies 264 = 6n \\implies n = 44\n\\]\n\nThe sum of an arithmetic series is given by the formula $S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a_1 + a_n)$, where $S_n$ is the sum of the first $n$ terms. So we have:\n\n\\[\nS_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \\cdot 260 = 5720\n\\]\n\nTo find the remainder when $5720$ is divided by $6$, we can find the remainder when $260$ is divided by $6$:\n\n\\[\n260 \\div 6 = 43 \\text{ remainder } 2\n\\]\n\nSo the remainder when $5720$ is divided by $6$ is the same as the remainder when $260$ is divided by $6$, which is $2$. Therefore, the remainder when the sum $1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259$ is divided by $6$ is $\\boxed{2}$.",
